From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: apple: t6050: Re-park a PIPE that a loader left on the T8103 dummy value

m1n1's usb_phy_bringup() writes PIPEHANDLER_MUX_CTRL = 0x22 before every
kernel handoff: dummy clock and data in the T8103 field layout, the USB4
clock with dummy data in the T6050 one. The cold park then refuses it and
dwc3-apple fails to probe:

  apple-t6050-dp-phy 2ab000000.phy: dummy PIPE park failed (-1): pipe
  00=00000000 04=00000016 0c=00000022 10=00000000 14=00000000 1c=00000010
  20=00009332
  dwc3-apple 2aa280000.usb: Failed to assert reset, err=-5

The park runs with the controller in reset and clamped, so no consumer
sees the clock change. Accept any state whose data select is off or dummy
and run the usual clock-off, dummy-data, dummy-clock sequence; a live
USB3 (0x10) or USB4 producer is still refused.

Fallback only: the loader-side fix (m1n1 0020) is preferred.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>

---
--- a/drivers/phy/apple/usb-t6050/apple_t6050_usb3_pipe.h	2026-11-06 18:13:57
+++ b/drivers/phy/apple/usb-t6050/apple_t6050_usb3_pipe.h	2026-11-06 18:13:57
@@ -23,10 +23,15 @@
     if (io->read(io->context, 44, 0x1c) & 1)
         return -1;
     mux = io->read(io->context, 44, 0x0c) & 0x73;
-    if (mux != 0 && mux != 2 && mux != 0x42)
-        return -1;
     if (mux == 0x42)
         return 0;
+    /*
+     * m1n1 writes the T8103-layout dummy value 0x22 (here: USB4 clock, dummy data) before
+     * every kernel handoff. The controller is in reset, so nothing consumes PIPE: re-park any
+     * state whose data select is off or dummy, and still refuse a live USB3/USB4 producer.
+     */
+    if (mux != 0 && (mux & 3) != 2)
+        return -1;
     apple_t6050_usb_mask(io, 44, 0x0c, 0x70, 0);
     io->delay(io->context, 10);
     apple_t6050_usb_mask(io, 44, 0x0c, 3, 2);
